    75	## Evidence boundary
    76	
    77	The code record establishes the consequences a grid operator may impose after repeated GTO breaches, but it does not allocate civil damages among the hub, a member, an installer and a software provider. ACM says that allocation is outside its power. No primary source found establishes that a blocked business park will pay the proposed diagnostic or recurring price; that an installer will preserve a separately priced wholesale line; or that a group will grant the required operating and evidence rights. Those questions remain the paid-test gates. Programme budgets and contract availability are not evidence of customer payment.

