chapters/07-eudi-wallet-acceptance.html:153:<nav class="chapter-nav">
chapters/05-product-passports.html:29:<p>The first customer is a Benelux company that assembles stationary energy-storage systems from batteries previously used in vehicles or other applications and expects to place its finished industrial batteries on the EU market after 18 February 2027. It is not a cell manufacturer or a vehicle OEM. It buys or receives donor packs or modules, tests and grades them, changes their purpose or configuration, integrates a BMS and enclosure, and becomes the economic operator for the second-life battery.</p>
chapters/05-product-passports.html:54:<p>The required production price is €30,000 for integration/onboarding, then €3,500 per month for managed evidence and change operations plus €12 per newly issued or materially updated passport event. These are hurdles, not market facts. The platform licence, identifier issuance, lab work and legal opinions are billed directly to the customer. If a ten-unit sprint cannot justify that next-stage order, do not assume thousands of future passports will.</p>
chapters/05-product-passports.html:124:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
chapters/06-grid-capacity-hubs.html:84:<p>The four tests are severe. Acquisition repeats only when partners originate qualified baselines without the founder's personal introductions. Delivery is teachable only when someone other than the founder can pass a simulated command-and-recovery test from the playbook. Value recurs only because allocations, equipment and constraints change. The asset accumulates only when the next compatible controller and agreement can be onboarded faster without exposing a prior site's data. If two of these fail, call it specialist integration work and price it accordingly; do not call it a software company.</p>
chapters/06-grid-capacity-hubs.html:135:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
chapters/03-machine-vision-food.html:41:<p>Buyer pain, legal duty and budget remain separate. A plant may accept manual checks because escapes are rare, buy a printer-integrated camera during the next replacement, or ask its incumbent integrator to add a smart camera. The first paid diagnostic must reveal the frequency and cost of holds, rework, retailer claims and code-related nonconformities at one line. Without those numbers, the regulation is merely atmosphere.</p>
chapters/03-machine-vision-food.html:109:<p>The team executes well. Two cheese packers pay for diagnostics. The optical design passes on glossy film, the reject path survives site acceptance, operators like the evidence log, and a respected Dutch integrator sells five cells. Then the integrator learns which dome, lens and thresholds work, while Domino supplies a printer-linked camera in the next fleet refresh. Customers prefer one service number and one recipe entry. The partner recreates the defect checklist in its existing platform and offers seal and film checks alongside the date for a modest premium. It honours every contract, simply stops ordering the module.</p>
chapters/03-machine-vision-food.html:145:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
TEMPLATE.md:29:Navigation: previous / contents / next. Use the shared static paths `../static/style.css` and
chapters/04-asset-intelligence.html:119:<nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Essay navigation">
chapters/02-white-label-product-security.html:82:<p>Acquisition repeats only when enabled partners originate qualified work without founder prospecting. Delivery is teachable only when another reviewer can reproduce a finding and the partner can explain it. Value recurs because components, releases, vulnerabilities and support state change. The asset accumulates only when the next engagement becomes faster without reusing confidential customer material. If quality requires the founder on every client call, the channel has multiplied meetings, not capacity.</p>
chapters/02-white-label-product-security.html:132:<nav class="chapter-nav">
chapters/01-connected-product-operations.html:80:<p>The four scalability tests are therefore explicit. Acquisition repeats only if two channels each create several paid baselines a year. Delivery is teachable only if analysts close most queue items from written procedures. Value recurs only while releases, vulnerabilities, requests and support states change. The asset accumulates only if integrations and evidence history reduce the next customer's labour. Fail any two and the honest outcome is a good expert practice, not a scalable company.</p>
chapters/01-connected-product-operations.html:129:<nav class="chapter-nav">

